  {
   "texts": [
    {
     "evidences": [
      {
       "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
       "source": "PubMed",
       "id": "32297921"
      }
     ],
     "value": "Specifically expressed in root nodules, and barely in pods"
    }
   ],
   "commentType": "TISSUE SPECIFICITY"
  },
  {
   "texts": [
    {
     "evidences": [
      {
       "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
       "source": "PubMed",
       "id": "32297921"
      }
     ],
     "value": "Gradual accumulation in developing and maturating root nodules (PubMed:32297921). Levels decline during nodule senescence (PubMed:32297921)"
    }
   ],
   "commentType": "DEVELOPMENTAL STAGE"
  },
  {
   "texts": [
    {
     "evidences": [
      {
       "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
       "source": "PubMed",
       "id": "18838253"
      },
      {
       "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
       "source": "PubMed",
       "id": "32297921"
      }
     ],
     "value": "Negatively regulated by cobalt (Co) in a dose-dependent manner (PubMed:18838253). Suppressed by exposure to excess nitrogen (N); this repression is associated with nodule greening and reduced biological nitrogen fixation (BN) efficiency (PubMed:32297921)"
    }
   ],
   "commentType": "INDUCTION"
  },
  {
   "texts": [
    {
     "evidences": [
      {
       "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250",
       "source": "UniProtKB",
       "id": "P02235"
      },
      {
       "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
       "source": "PubMed",
       "id": "22308405"
      }
     ],
     "value": "Nitrated mainly at Tyr-31 and, to a lower extent, at Tyr-26 and Tyr-134, in effective nodules and particularly in hypoxic conditions; this mechanism may play a protective role in the symbiosis by buffering toxic peroxynitrite NO(2)(-) (PubMed:22308405). Nitration level decrease during nodule senescence (By similarity)"
    }
   ],
   "commentType": "PTM"
  },
  {
   "texts": [
    {
     "evidences": [
      {
       "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250",
       "source": "UniProtKB",
       "id": "Q3C1F7"
      }
     ],
     "value": "Phosphorylation at Ser-46 disrupts the molecular environment of its porphyrin ring oxygen binding pocket, thus leading to a reduced oxygen consumption and to the delivery of oxygen O(2) to symbiosomes"
    }
   ],
   "commentType": "PTM"
  },
  {
   "texts": [
    {
     "evidences": [
      {
       "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305"
      }
     ],
     "value": "Belongs to the plant globin family"
    }
   ],
   "commentType": "SIMILARITY"
  }
